WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:01.923
- In many parts of the world,

00:00:01.923 --> 00:00:04.110
Scrabble is viewed as a pastime,

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:06.704
as a game where, maybe old people play

00:00:06.704 --> 00:00:08.416
after retirement and all that,

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.293
but Scrabble in Nigeria
is actually very big.

00:00:12.293 --> 00:00:14.718
It is seen as a sport.

00:00:14.718 --> 00:00:17.294
There is an actual Nigerian
Scrabble Federation

00:00:17.294 --> 00:00:18.869
under the Ministry of Sports.

00:00:18.869 --> 00:00:20.538
They have a lot of young people

00:00:20.538 --> 00:00:23.911
hoping to earn an actual
living from playing Scrabble.

00:00:23.911 --> 00:00:25.687
My name is Wellington Jighere

00:00:25.687 --> 00:00:28.687
and I'm the world Scrabble champion.

00:00:31.335 --> 00:00:33.510
I started playing Scrabble in 1996

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.120
when my immediate elder
brother taught me the game.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.849
It wasn't until six years after that,

00:00:38.849 --> 00:00:42.639
I was playing with some
of my neighborhood friends

00:00:42.639 --> 00:00:44.996
and they were like,
"Ah, you are quite good.

00:00:44.996 --> 00:00:47.248
"Why not play in tournaments?"

00:00:47.248 --> 00:00:48.263
And I was like,

00:00:48.263 --> 00:00:50.183
"Wow, you mean they play
this in tournaments?"

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.933
The rest is history, as they say.

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:56.749
Having an African win the
World Scrabble Championship

00:00:56.749 --> 00:00:58.842
is bigger than I can actual comprehend.

00:00:58.842 --> 00:01:00.554
You needed to have been in the hall

00:01:00.554 --> 00:01:04.642
to see the jubilation of
our other African brothers.

00:01:04.642 --> 00:01:06.872
It was something that everyone in Africa

00:01:06.872 --> 00:01:09.685
that plays Scrabble has
actually looked forward to.

00:01:09.685 --> 00:01:13.737
Nigeria is a very, very diverse nation.

00:01:13.737 --> 00:01:16.291
We have well over 500 developed languages,

00:01:16.291 --> 00:01:18.773
but the major means of communication

00:01:18.773 --> 00:01:20.693
all over Nigeria is English,

00:01:20.693 --> 00:01:23.255
and since Scrabble is based
upon the English vocabulary,

00:01:23.255 --> 00:01:26.485
it's going to be a way of
helping each and everyone

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:30.318
improve their command
of the English language.

00:01:33.116 --> 00:01:34.606
If I hadn't played Scrabble,

00:01:34.606 --> 00:01:36.390
I might have been involved in

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:39.850
some of the not so legitimate activities,

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.376
and I think playing Scrabble,

00:01:41.376 --> 00:01:44.586
it keeps you on the right track.

00:01:44.586 --> 00:01:48.728
We are not blind to the fact
that the level of unemployment

00:01:48.728 --> 00:01:51.500
in the country is very, very immense,

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.191
so I came up with the
Wellington Foundation

00:01:54.191 --> 00:01:56.495
for Scrabble and Mind
Development in Africa.

00:01:56.495 --> 00:01:59.696
There's a lot of similarities between

00:01:59.696 --> 00:02:03.772
how life actually goes
and how Scrabble goes.

00:02:03.772 --> 00:02:05.489
You get to understand that it's not

00:02:05.489 --> 00:02:07.536
all the time that you get things your way.

00:02:07.536 --> 00:02:09.721
You really have to make the best

00:02:09.721 --> 00:02:12.660
out of the little that you are given.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:16.719
You know, each country is
known for a particular sport.

00:02:16.719 --> 00:02:18.850
Brazil, for example,
is known for football.

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:22.129
We're hoping to make
Scrabble a Nigerian sport.

00:02:22.129 --> 00:02:25.366
If you mention Scrabble
in any part of the world,

00:02:25.366 --> 00:02:27.699
Nigeria should come to mind.

